WEBVTT

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.040
You're still awake?

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:42.290
I couldn't sleep. Neither could you?

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:46.290
He said he'd go convince his dad,
but can he pull it off?

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.000
If he can't...

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.700
He'll probably step down.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.000
Oh no! The five of us worked
so hard together to get this far!

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:01.000
The costumes will go to waste, too.
What's that idiot doing?!

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.410
Tenma!

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.410
I'm back.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.000
"My Weakness"

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.750
"My Weakness"
That's cold.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.040
"My Weakness"
You okay?

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.290
"My Weakness"
Looks painful.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.000
Looking handsome.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.700
How did it go with your dad?

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:58.120
He gave me a good wallop, as you can see.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.370
Because you joined a theater troupe
without telling?

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:03.870
No, 'cause I turned down
the movie offer without permission.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:10.700
We had a serious talk after I
apologized for that, and I convinced him.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:17.410
This play is a crucial step
for my acting career.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.540
Because you have no prior stage experience?

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.830
No...

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.080
I need to tell you guys something.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.040
What?

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:34.040
My first play was in elementary school
at a school arts festival.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:38.080
By then, I had already been in
films and TV dramas,

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.200
--Ready, go... Peter Pan!
--so a play for a school arts festival
should've been easy.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.950
But then...

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:54.450
...my mind went blank,
and I forgot all my lines.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:04:00.120
I froze on the spot, speechless,
while the audience went silent.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:10.660
The time it took for the curtain to close
felt like an eternity.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.790
People around me encouraged me,
blaming it on my busy work schedule.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.910
But I'd never made a blunder like for work.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.870
It was the first time I tasted humiliation.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:28.660
After that, even if I got offers for plays,
I always declined out of fear.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.620
That feeling comes back just standing on stage.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.370
Like you get nervous?

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.950
It's not nerves. It's more like fear.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.080
I might just be a coward.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.040
Afraid?

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.000
You, Tenma?

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.950
For movies and TV,
you can redo a scene multiple times

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.450
until you get the perfect cut.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.370
I can present only the perfect
and best me without compromise.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:58.700
But on stage, I get one chance in that moment
to show my performance.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:03.330
I freaked out when I realized this
during my school play.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:09.700
I see. You want to show people
your best performance every time.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:14.080
But that doesn't make you a coward.
You just have high standards as a pro.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.040
I think it's a great trait
to possess as an actor.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:22.040
All the same, I want to overcome
this fear no matter what.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:25.830
Let me stand on the stage
together with everyone.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.200
Tenma...

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.000
Tenten...

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.450
What are you talking about, hack?

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:36.000
You came back, so there's no way we'd drop you.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.750
Tenma, the show can't get started
without our leader--

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.200
Why're you surprised?!

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.620
You <i>can </i>call me "Tenma."

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:45.830
Seriously?!

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:49.330
Tenten, we're doing this play
together with you for sure!

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.120
We're buds, and you know it!

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:56.080
That's right. It's thanks to you
that our acting's improved so much.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.200
Tenma.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.950
Have this hyper triangle to give you courage!

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:09.450
Where'd you get that from? Put it back!

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:11.000
Aw.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:19.580
Thanks, guys.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.830
Glad to be working with you again, Yuki.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.620
What?! "Yuki"?!

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.250
Gross!

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.700
You said it first!

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:30.580
I have no idea what you're talking about, <i>hack</i>.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:33.910
I know you can overcome your fear.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:36.910
Yeah...

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.500
It's true that on stage, you can't give
a perfect and ideal performance each time.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.830
But you <i>can </i>give the best performance.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.910
What do you mean?

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.700
You'll understand once you get on stage.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.540
Gotta sell those tickets for you, Tenten.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:54.410
Can you add this as a bonus?

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.540
--Too big.
--Aw.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.080
"Veludo Station"

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.290
"Veludo Station"
The run for new Summer Troupe's show
at Mankai Company is starting soon!

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:09.870
The run for new Summer Troupe's show
at Mankai Company is starting soon!

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:12.660
This triangle's for you!

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:17.410
A comedy based on <i>The Arabian Nights</i>.
Please come watch!

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.450
Please come watch.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:21.580
Hey, doesn't he look like Tenma Sumeragi?

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.330
--What, really?
--Please come watch.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.080
--Heya!
--Want one?

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.830
Sorry, I'm heading elsewhere to flyer.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:32.620
Okay, leave this area to me and Sumi.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.290
We're Mankai Company. Please come watch!

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:42.250
Our production of <i>Water me!</i>
starts in a few days!

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.410
Hey, is that Rurikawa?

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:48.160
Yeah, it is Rurikawa!

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.000
You still dressing like a girl?

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.540
Hilarious. You look good.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.450
You dress as girly as your name sounds.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.410
What're you doing? Passing out flyers
for a cross-dressing cafe?

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.370
H-Hey, what's your problem?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.040
Muku, it's fine.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.250
Yuki...

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.410
Who's this? Your cross-dressing buddy?

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:11.950
Hilarious! Man, "birds of a feather fl--"

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.700
Not a cross-dressing cafe. A play.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.540
Here's the flyer for our show.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:17.830
A play...?

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.330
Yes.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.580
Then, I will spin another tale for you tonight.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:30.200
One of a thousand tales
that capture the imagination.

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:35.000
Wh-What the heck?

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.330
A sneak peak of our play.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:41.830
Here, take one. Better come on closing night.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.790
Oh, I guess if it's acting...

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:49.700
Y-Yeah. As long as it's not
a cross-dressing cafe... it works.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.410
Yeah, it works.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.250
Please come!

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:00.750
Yuki.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:02.950
Let's take a break.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.000
Y-Yeah!

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.910
You really are cool, Yuki.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.040
Huh?! What about me?!

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.290
What you just did...

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.830
That? I was just copying
God Troupe's fan service.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.000
Yeah, but you looked cool.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:32.450
You looked so cool.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.620
Yeah.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:39.700
Come here for a sec.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:41.200
'Kay.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:51.910
You're so cool, because even in that situation,

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:55.910
you could boldly say what you said.
It's why I look up to you.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:10:00.620
Stop it already. I get it.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:01.950
Okay.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.580
Thanks.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.410
Yeah.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:11.250
Let's work hard for our performance.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.160
Of course.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.700
Yeah?

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.450
Tenten, what's up?

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:29.910
Add my photo to our official site.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.500
What?! You cool with it?!

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.620
Yeah.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.450
I'm gonna write "Tenma Sumeragi."

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:42.660
Yeah, that's fine.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.290
Alrighty, this'll be quick!

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.370
Yeah! And update!

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.700
Director!

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:57.950
Oh no!

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:00.500
Manager, what's wrong?

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:07.160
You see, there was sudden influx in
ticket sales, and we were instantly sold out!

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.620
Sold out?!

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:12.910
We sold out of all our remaining tickets
in just about ten minutes!

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:14.910
We also have a full house for closing night!

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:17.040
Is that because...

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:21.120
Extra triangles.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:26.790
That's why I told that idiot
to do this in the first place.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.910
Hello, this is Mankai Company.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.870
What?! An interview?!

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:36.830
Er... I'll send you the details
of our dress rehearsal by fax.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.330
Yes! Thank you!

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.500
Hello? Yes!

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:46.950
--I can send you the details
of our dress rehearsal again by fax.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:47.700
--I can send you the details
of our dress rehearsal again by fax.
--This whole thing is going crazy.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:48.910
--Yes. That's right!
--This whole thing is going crazy.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:49.500
--Yes. That's right!
--The phone's ringing nonstop.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.160
--Thank you and see you soon!
--The phone's ringing nonstop.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:54.120
--He's scurrying around.
--Yes! This is Mankai Company.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:56.870
Sounds like the press is coming.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.830
Anyway, let's work hard on
the finishing touches for dress rehearsal!

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:02.200
--Yeah!
--Yes, ma'am!

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:11.870
I can't believe that Tenma Sumeragi,
prominent in movies and TV, is doing theater.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:15.160
You could say this is the moment
we've all been waiting for.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.830
At any rate, I look forward to what we'll see.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:21.660
Shoot, there's tons of cams.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:24.290
Looks like something you'd see on TV.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.000
So many people!

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.120
Is it always like this?

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:30.410
Earth to Tenma!

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:31.540
Hm?

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:34.290
The hack is back.

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:35.160
Ah.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:36.950
What do you mean, "ah"?!

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:40.540
Tenma, are you all right?

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:42.830
Everyone, please be on standby!

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:44.410
Oh, right!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.750
Get ready, everyone!

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.330
You, too, Tenma.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:58.620
Thank you for coming to
the dress rehearsal of <i>Water me!</i>

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:05.330
presented to you by
Mankai Company's Summer Troupe.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:08.450
Please sit back and enjoy the show.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.500
Tonight I have another tale to share with you.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:29.700
One of a thousand tales
that capture the imagination.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:37.830
His name is Ali Baba, a poor, hardworking
young man who dreams of becoming rich.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:39.830
And I am...

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:51.700
Tell me, Scheherazade!
Where is the legendary paradise Oasis?!

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:57.910
Then, I will spin another tale for you tonight.
Long ago, in a faraway land--

00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:01.910
J-Just cut to the chase!
Give it to me in four words or less!

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:06.410
Aladdin. Magic lamp. Magician.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:15.160
You're Sinbad, aren't you?
Shouldn't you know where the gold is already?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:20.830
O-Oh, grow up, Ali Baba.
There <i>is </i>no legendary paradise.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:21.540
--You're not going to get rich quick.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:24.950
--They're all so worried about Tenma
that they can't focus.
--You're not going to get rich quick.

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:27.080
Try some honest work for a change.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:36.750
This is an important scene where Scheherazade
confesses the truth to Ali Baba.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:41.120
I've stalled things so far,
but my hands are tied now.

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:44.540
I must join the king's harem.

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:46.250
Is that--

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:55.040
Huh?

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.000
Did he blank on his line?!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.750
Tenten!

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:02.540
Tenma...

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:05.120
--What's this?
--Is this part of the play?

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:10.410
Are you that shocked? Well, I don't blame you.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.620
Nice save, Yukki!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.200
That kept it going.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.040
--It doesn't matter now anyway. Forget about me.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:16.580
--But...
--It doesn't matter now anyway. Forget about me.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.410
--It doesn't matter now anyway. Forget about me.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:19.660
Mm...

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.950
I don't know about this...

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:44.910
Hey, guys, you weren't at the top of
your game for today's dress rehearsal.

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:48.620
But let's change gears and try to get
back in top condition for opening night!

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:51.080
Yeah, it's no biggie!

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:52.620
Y-Yeah, that's right!

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.540
Yup!

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:57.660
Lose the gloomy face.

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:59.000
Oh, man!

00:15:59.000 --> 00:15:59.830
What's the matter?

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:03.370
Uh, i-it's nothing.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:04.500
Stuff online?

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.450
It's nothing, really!

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:07.410
Yukki!

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.370
Hey, wai--

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:11.500
An article on our dress rehearsal.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.410
I said it's nothing!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:18.450
"A Poor Start: Premature Debut
for the Silver Screen Prince?"

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:20.450
What? That's terrible.

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:23.290
Dude, stop, Yukki!

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:27.250
Well, this is the harsh reality.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.250
So sad...

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:35.370
Th-The real thing's tomorrow.
We've still got time, so it's all good!

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:39.500
But we need to step it up, huh?

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:43.830
We don't need to have a meeting or anything?

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.120
No.

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:48.040
Tenma...

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:55.250
Tenma hasn't given up already, has he?

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:57.830
Tenten wouldn't give up so fast!

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.000
I hope not.

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:15.790
"Tenten, you okay?"
"I'm super worried! Anyway, hit me back!"
"Where are you?"
"Everyone's waiting for you! Me included!"

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:21.450
Grandpa.

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:26.290
Acting's fun, just like you said, Grandpa.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:33.330
I want to keep acting more with everyone!

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:41.410
Where did that idiot go?

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.910
Is that what you want?!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:51.040
If you'd just talked to me instead of
making up some cockamamie tale--

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:59.580
Sorry. Am I interrupting?

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:00.500
It's fine.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.620
Can we talk a moment?

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:03.910
Yeah.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:08.660
Still thinking about the dress rehearsal, huh?

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.700
I didn't think...

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:18.120
...I could mess up worse than
what happened at my school play.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.250
I was wrong.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.160
That was nothing!

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.410
For me, I was bound to always skip some lines.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:30.290
I even said a different character's lines
for an entire play.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.620
What?!

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:34.330
I came onto stage when it wasn't my scene.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.950
Another time, I tripped and tore off
the lead's clothes as I fell.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.870
Are you serious?

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:40.540
Completely.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:44.000
So your blunders were nothing compared to mine!

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:47.580
I'm surprised you still did theater after that.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:58.450
I'm afraid to go on stage again tomorrow...
afraid I might humiliate myself again.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:08.750
But the shows I messed up on
drew the biggest laughs from the audience.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.080
I'm not saying I'm glad I messed up,

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:17.080
but those were the times that
I made the crowd roar with laughter.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:23.790
There's no rule that says you can't make
mistakes or hesitate when you're on stage.

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:30.790
Even if it's not perfect, if you can get
the best laughs from it, that's the best show.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.910
To give the best show even if it's not perfect?

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:44.250
I'm just a hammy actor, but my heart pounded
every time before I'd go on stage.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.080
You said so yourself, Tenma.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:50.790
That unlike TV and film,
you only get one chance on stage.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:56.120
The audience comes to see a show
that will only ever happen once.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:01.830
To see the best performance.
To have the best time.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:09.750
So you don't always have to
give a perfect performance.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:13.410
On stage, all you need to do is keep growing.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:18.200
It's where you can boundlessly expand
and redefine what your "very best" is.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.580
As long as you're on stage,

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:24.450
you can keep creating
the best shows again and again.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:32.830
You really say some amazing things.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:39.620
Nobody laughed when I talked about
my school play. Not you or the others.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:43.000
You figured out that the
reason behind my weakness

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.500
was because I wanted to give
the perfect performance.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:52.080
You're the first one to
accept my weakness like you did.

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:53.700
Tenma...

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.910
Snuck off here with just the two of you?

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:01.330
Is that what Tenma and the director were doing?!

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:03.250
Tenten, no fair getting a head start on us!

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:05.040
Let me play, too!

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:08.000
I-I don't know how I feel about
being the romantic foil...

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.950
Oh, but that might also be exciting!

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:14.830
What? Why the hell are you guys--whoa!

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:18.250
Aren't we going to practice?

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.370
Tenten, let's practice together!

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:23.540
Yeah, I want to smooth out
the rough spots before the show!

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:25.080
Me, too!

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.330
Man, you guys!

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:32.790
Come on, let's get started.

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:35.200
Practice time!

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:56.500
So, which part?

00:21:57.370 --> 00:22:01.200
The whole thing. We're gonna
get this thing down today!

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:03.660
The hack's super motivated again.

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:05.330
What'd you say?!

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:07.700
--None of them have given up.
--Let go of my hand! Gross!

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:09.290
I saw that grin.

00:22:09.290 --> 00:22:10.370
Say, what?!

00:22:10.370 --> 00:22:12.660
--I'm sure they can bounce back!
--Let's all do our best!

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:15.080
Hip hip hooray!

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:17.000
Hooray!
